<title>USA: AlliedSignal unit gets Bombardier contract.</title>
<headline>AlliedSignal unit gets Bombardier contract.</headline>
<dateline>TORRANCE, Calif. 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>AlliedSignal Inc said Thursday its Aerospace unit had won a contract from Bombardier Inc valued at more than $250 million.</p>
<p>The contract is for design, development and certification of the auxiliary power unit (APU) system for more than 400 new regional aircraft Bombardier expects to produce.  </p>
<p>The APU will provide compressed air for air conditioning and main engine starting as well as power to drive an air conditioning electrical generator.</p>
